hadiths[60]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20255","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to me, and Ibn Abi Bukayr, meaning Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, the meaning, he said: I heard Abu Qazaah narrating to Amr ibn Dinar from Hakim ibn Muawiyah al-Bahzi from his father that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I swore thus, and he spread the fingers of his hands, until you inform me what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent you with. He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent me with Islam. He said: And what is Islam? He said: Testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and you establish prayer and give zakat."
"20256","Two assisting brothers: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept from anyone repentance who associates partners after his Islam."
"20257","He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of ones wife upon him? He said: You feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except in the house."
"20258","Then he said: Here you will be gathered, here you will be gathered, here you will be gathered, three times, riding and walking and upon your faces."
"20259","You will complete on the Day of Resurrection seventy nations; you are the last of nations and the most noble of them upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"20260","You will come on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles upon your mouths; the first thing to speak for one of you is his thigh. Ibn Abi Bukayr said: He pointed with his hand toward al-Sham and said: To here you will be gathered."
"20261","Muhanna ibn Abd al-Hamid Abu Shibl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Qazaah from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man among those before you, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, had granted him wealth and children until an era passed and an era came, and when death came to him he said: O my sons, what kind of father was I to you? They said: The best father. He said: Are you obedient to me? They said: Yes. He said: See, when I die, burn me until you leave me as charcoal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So they did that, then crush me with the mortar, gesturing with his hand. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So they did, by Allah, that, then scatter me in the sea on a windy day, perhaps I may escape Allah, Blessed and Exalted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So they did, by Allah, that, and behold he was in the grasp of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and He said: O son of Adam, what carried you to what you did? He said: O Lord, fear of You. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, pardoned him thereby."
"20262","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Qazaah from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man asked him: What is the right of a wife upon the husband? He said: You feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except in the house."
"20263","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Qazaah Suwayd ibn Hujayr al-Bahili informed us, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father that his brother Malik said: O Muawiyah, Muhammad has taken my neighbors, so go to him, for he knows you and has spoken to you. He said: So I went with him, and he said: Leave me my neighbors, for they had embraced Islam, so he turned away from him. He stood up strutting and said: By Allah, if you do, people claim you command a matter and turn to other than it. I kept dragging him while he talked, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What does he say? They said: By Allah, if you do that, people claim you command a matter and oppose it to other than it. He said: So he said: Have they said it, or the sayer of them; if I did that, it is only upon me, and nothing of that is upon them; release his neighbors to him."
"20264","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And you complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and most noble upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"20265","Ismail Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For every grazing camels, for every forty a bint labun; camels are not separated from their reckoning; whoever gives it seeking reward, he has its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it from him and half his camels as a binding decree of our Lord, Mighty and Majestic; nothing of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad."
"20266","Ismail narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us, from his father from his grandfather that his father or his uncle stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: For what were my neighbors taken? He turned away from him, then said: Inform me for what they were taken, so he turned away from him. He said: If you say that, they claim you forbid wrongdoing and seclude yourself with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did he say? His brother or his nephew stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, he said. He said: You have said it, or your sayer; if I were to do that, it is upon me and not upon you; release his neighbors to him."
"20267","Abu Kamil narrated to us, from Hammad, Abu Qazaah narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam."
"20268","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized people of my tribe on accusation and detained them, so a man of my tribe came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he preached and said: O Muhammad, for what do you detain my neighbors? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward him. He said: People say you forbid evil and seclude yourself with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What does he say? He said: So I kept intervening between them with speech fearing he would hear it and supplicate against my tribe a supplication after which they would never succeed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept at him until he understood it, then said: They have said it, or a sayer among them; by Allah, if I did, it would be upon me and would not be upon them; release his neighbors to him."
"20269","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever his freedman asks him for surplus of his wealth and he does not give him, it will be made on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent."
"20270","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to one who narrates to people then lies to make them laugh; woe to him, and woe to him."
"20271","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Qazaah al-Bahili informed us, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I did not come to you until I swore the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you; Affan showed us joining his palms; by the One who sent you with truth, what did He send you with? He said: Islam. He said: And what is Islam? He said: That your heart submit to Allah, Exalted, and you turn your face to Allah, Exalted, and pray the prescribed prayer and give the obligatory zakat."
"20272","Two assisting brothers: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept from anyone repentance who associates partners after his Islam."
"20273","I said: What is the right of ones wife upon him? He said: You feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except in the house."
"20274","He said: You will be gathered here, and he gestured with his hand toward al-Sham, walking and riding and upon your faces."
"20275","You will be presented to Allah, Exalted, with muzzles upon your mouths, and the first thing to speak for one of you is his thigh."
"20276","And he said: There is no freedman who comes to a freedman of his asking him from surplus with him and he withholds it, but Allah, Exalted, will make it upon him a serpent that bites him before the reckoning. Affan said: Meaning by mawla his cousin."
"20277","He said: And he said: A man among those before you, Allah, Exalted, had granted him wealth and children until an era passed and another came, and when he was dying he said to his children: What kind of father was I to you? They said: The best father. He said: Are you obedient to me, otherwise I will take my wealth from you? See, when I die, burn me until you leave me as coal, then crush me with the mortar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his hands opposite his knees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So they did, by Allah, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his hand thus, then scatter me on a windy day, perhaps I may escape Allah, Exalted, thus Affan said. My father said, and Muhanna Abu Shibl said from Hammad: escape Allah. So they did, by Allah, that, and behold he was standing in the grasp of Allah, Exalted, and He said: O son of Adam, what carried you to what you did? He said: From fear of You. So Allah, Exalted, pardoned him thereby."
"20278","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Hammad in what I heard, he said: And I heard al-Jurayri narrating from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and most noble upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and between the two leaves of a gate of Paradise is a forty-year journey, and a day will come upon it when it is crowded."
"20279","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri Abu Masud informed us, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You will come on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles upon your mouths, and the first thing to speak of the son of Adam is his thigh and his palm."
"20280","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu Qazaah informed us, from a man of Banu Qushayr from his father that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is the right of my wife upon me? He said: You feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, and do not abandon except in the house."
"20281","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from his father from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall I honor? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Your mother. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then whom? He said: Your mother. He said: I said: Then whom? He said: Then your father, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"20282","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz informed us, from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Verily you complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and most noble upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"20283","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz informed us, from his father from his grandfather who said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, our women, what do we partake of them and what do we leave? He said: Your tilth, come to your tilth as you wish, except do not strike the face, nor revile, nor abandon except in the house, and feed when you eat and clothe when you clothe yourself, how, when some of you has been intimate with some, except by what became lawful upon her."
"20284","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz informed us, from his father from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where do you command me? He said: Here, and he gestured with his hand toward al-Sham. He said: You will be gathered as men and riders, and dragged upon your faces."
"20285","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us, from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man comes to his mawla asking him from surplus with him and he withholds it from him, but a serpent licking its lips will be called for him on the Day of Resurrection, his surplus which he withheld."
"20286","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us, from his father from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people who ask of one another our wealth. He said: A man asks in calamity or rupture to reconcile between his people thereby, then when it reaches or is near, he refrains."
"20287","Yahya ibn Said and Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Bahz, he said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private parts, what do we partake of them and what do we leave? He said: Guard your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when people are among one another? He said: If you can that no one sees it, then let none see it. I said: When one of us is alone? He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more worthy to be shy of."
"20288","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Bahz, then he mentioned the like, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more worthy to be shy of, and he placed his hand upon his private part."
"20289","Yunus narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd who said also, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his hand and placed it upon his private part."
"20290","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Bahz, he said: My father informed me from my grandfather who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I did not come to you until I swore more than the number of these, striking one hand upon the other, that I would not come to you nor come to your religion, and I have come as a man who understands nothing except what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger taught me, and I ask you by the face of Allah, with what did our Lord send you to us? He said: With Islam. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the sign of Islam? He said: That you say: I submitted my face to Allah and divested, and establish prayer and give zakat, and every Muslim is inviolable to a Muslim."
"20291","Two assisting brothers: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept from a polytheist who associates partners after he embraced Islam a deed, or: he separates from the polytheists to the Muslims."
"20292","Why do I hold your waist-wrappers from the Fire? Verily my Lord calls me and will ask me: Did you convey to My servants? And I will say to Him: Lord, I conveyed to them. Let the witness among you convey to the absent."
"20293","Then you will be called, with your mouths bridled with muzzles, and the first thing to clarify, and he said in Wasit: to translate, he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his hand upon his thigh. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is our religion? He said: This is your religion, and wherever you do good it suffices you."
"20294","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Bahz narrated to us, my father narrated to me from my grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For every grazing camels, for every forty a bint labun; camels are not separated from their reckoning; whoever gives it seeking reward, he has its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half his camels as a binding decree of our Lord, Blessed and Exalted; nothing of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad."
"20295","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Bahz narrated to us, and Yazid said: Bahz informed us, the meaning, my father narrated to me from my grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was a servant of Allahs servants to whom Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gave wealth and children, and he did not observe Allahs religion, Mighty and Majestic. Yazid said: He remained until an age passed and an age remained; he remembered and knew he had not stored good with Allah, Blessed and Exalted, so he called his sons: O my sons, what kind of father do you know? They said: The best, O our father. He said: By Allah, I will not leave with a man among you wealth of mine except I take it from him, or you do what I command you. He took a covenant from them. He said: Verily not; when I die, take me and cast me in fire until I am coal, then crush me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his hand upon his thigh as if saying: Grind me, then scatter me in the wind, perhaps I may escape Allah, Blessed and Exalted. He said: So it was done with him, by the Lord of Muhammad, when he died. He said: So he was brought in the best form he was, and presented to his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and He said: What carried you to the fire? He said: Fear of You, O my Lord. He said: I hear the fear, Yazid said: I hear you fearful, so he was pardoned. Bahz said: I narrated this hadith to al-Hasan and Qatadah and they narrated it to me: So he was pardoned, or: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, turned to him; Yahya doubted."
"20296","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private parts, what do we partake of them and what do we leave? He said: Guard your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses. I said: What if people are among one another? He said: If you can that no one sees it, then let none see it. I said: What if one of us is alone? He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more worthy to be shy of than people."
"20297","Ismail narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For every grazing camels, for every forty a bint labun; camels are not separated from their reckoning; whoever gives it seeking reward, he has its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it from him and half his wealth, and he said once: his camels, as a binding decree of our Lord, Blessed and Exalted; nothing of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad."
"20298","Ismail narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us, from his father from his grandfather that his brother or his uncle stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: For what were my neighbors taken? He turned away from him. He said: For what were my neighbors taken? He turned away from him, then said: For what were my neighbors taken? He turned away from him. He said: If you say that, people have claimed that Muhammad forbids wrongdoing and secludes himself with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did he say? His brother or his nephew stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, he, he. He said: Verily you have said it, or your sayer said; if I were to do that, it is upon me and not upon you; release his neighbors to him."
"20299","Ismail narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us, from his father from his grandfather that I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I came to him and said: By Allah, I did not come to you until I swore more than the number of these that I would not come to you nor come to your religion, and Bahz joined his palms, and I have come as a man who understands nothing except what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and His Messenger taught me, and I ask you by the face of Allah, with what did Allah send you to us? He said: With Islam. I said: And what are the signs of Islam? He said: That you say: I submitted my face to Allah and divested, and establish prayer and give zakat; every Muslim is inviolable to a Muslim."
"20300","Two assisting brothers: Allah does not accept from a polytheist who associates partners after he embraced Islam a deed, and you separate from the polytheists to the Muslims."
"20301","What is the matter with me that I hold your waistbands back from the Fire? Verily my Lord Almighty is calling me, and He will ask me whether I conveyed to His servants, and I will say: My Lord, I have conveyed to them, so let the present among you convey to the absent."
"20302","Then you will be summoned with your mouths muzzled with muzzles, then the first thing that will speak for one of you will be his thigh and his palm. I said: O Prophet of Allah, is this our religion? He said: This is your religion, and wherever you do good it will suffice you."
"20303","Ismail narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim ibn Muawiyah narrated to us from his father from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was a servant among the servants of Allah Almighty to whom Allah gave wealth and children, and he did not observe any religion toward Allah Blessed and Exalted. He remained until when his life had gone or remained, he remembered and knew that he would not acquire any good with Allah Blessed and Exalted. He called his sons and said: What kind of father do you know me to be? They said: The best, O our father. He said: By Allah, I will not leave with any of you wealth that is from me except that I take it from him, and you shall do to me what I command you. So he took a covenant from them, by my Lord. He said: When I die, throw me into the fire until I become charred coals, then crush me, and it is as if I look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he says with his hand upon his thigh, then scatter me in the wind so that I may escape Allah Blessed and Exalted. He said: They did that to him, by the Lord of Muhammad, when he died. Then he was brought in the best form he had ever been, and was presented to his Lord Blessed and Exalted. He said: What drove you to the fire? He said: Your fear, O my Lord. He said: I hear you are indeed fearful, so He forgave him."
"20304","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Bahz ibn Hakim ibn Muawiyah ibn Haydah al-Qushayri, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, our women, what may we approach of them and what should we leave? He said: Your tilth, approach your tilth as you wish, provided you do not strike the face nor revile, and feed when you are fed and clothe when you clothe, and do not forsake except in the house. How so when some of you have gone into one another except by what has become lawful for them."
"20305","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Bahz ibn Hakim, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the one who speaks and lies to make the people laugh thereby, woe to him."
"20306","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Bahz ibn Hakim, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man comes to a freed slave of his asking him from surplus he has and he withholds it, except a bald serpent will be called for him on the Day of Resurrection licking with its tongue the surplus he withheld."
"20307","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Bahz narrated to us, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I be dutiful? He said: Your mother. He said: I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. He said: I said: Then whom? He said: Your mother, then your father, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"20308","Yahya narrated to us from Bahz, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You have completed seventy nations, you are the last of them and the noblest of them to Allah Almighty."
"20309","Yahya narrated to us from Bahz, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where do you command me, choose for me. He pointed with his hand toward Sham and said: You will be gathered on foot and mounted, and you will be dragged upon your faces."
"20310","Yahya narrated to us from Bahz, he said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people who ask one another for our wealth. He said: One of you asks in calamity and rupture to reconcile between his people, then when it reaches or nears, he refrains."
"20311","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us from Hakim ibn Muawiyah Abu Bahz from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Paradise are the sea of milk and the sea of water and the sea of honey and the sea of wine, then the rivers split from them afterwards."
"20312","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Qazah al-Bahili from Hakim ibn Muawiyah from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Allah after his Islam."
"20313","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us from his father from his grandfather, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought something, he asked about it: Is it a gift or charity? If they said: A gift, he extended his hand, and if they said: Charity, he said to his companions: Take."
"20314","Yazid narrated to us, Bahz informed us from his father from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the one who speaks and lies to make the people laugh thereby, woe to him, woe to him."
